e world’s most influential books. During the thirteenth century, the Persian naturalist and judge Zakariyyāʾ Qazwīnī authored what became one of the most influential works of natural history in the world: Wonders and Rarities. Exploring the dazzling movements of the stars above, the strange minutiae of the minerals beneath the earth, and everything in between, Qazwīnī offered a captivating account of the cosmos. With fine paintings and leading science, Wonders and Rarities inspired generations as it traveled through madrasas and courts, unveiling the magical powers of nature. Yet after circulating for centuries, first in Arabic and Persian, then in Turkish and Urdu, Qazwīnī’s compendium eventually came to stand as a strange, if beautiful, emblem of medieval ignorance.","pageCount":465,"publicationYear":2023,"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"History","sourceId":"source-google-books-summary-wonders-and-rarities-the-marvelous-book-that-traveled-the-world-and-mapped-the-cosmos-travis-zad"}],"displaySummary":"With fine paintings and leading science, Wonders and Rarities inspired generations as it traveled through madrasas and courts, unveiling the magical powers of nature. Yet after circulating for centuries, first in Arabic and Persian, then in Turkish and Urdu, Qazwīnī’s compendium eventually came to stand as a strange, if beautiful, emblem of medieval ignorance.","primaryTopic":"Natural History & Animals","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"World History","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"World History","score":8,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"llm_classifier","rawLabel":"World History","mappedSubject":"World History","score":8,"confidence":"high","note":"The book primarily explores the historical significance and impact of Qazwīnī's work on natural history within a transnational context.","id":"subject-evidence-book-wonders-and-rarities-the-marvelous-book-that-tr